# Every pattern here is ANCHORED to the repo root with a leading slash.
#
# That is deliberate, not stylistic. An unanchored pattern like `sourcemap.json`
# also matches `ServerPackages/_Index/.../profilestore/sourcemap.json`, which
# ships inside a vendored package. Silently dropping a file out of a committed
# dependency tree defeats the whole reason those trees are committed.

# Regenerated on demand by `rojo sourcemap`. Never committed - it encodes
# tree state and would conflict on every branch.
/sourcemap.json

# Build artifacts
/build/
/*.rbxl
/*.rbxlx
/*.rbxm
/*.rbxmx
/*.rbxl.lock
/*.rbxlx.lock

# Claude Code local overrides - machine-specific, never shared
/.claude/settings.local.json
/CLAUDE.local.md

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
/.vscode/settings.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED - do not "clean this up":
#
#   Packages/ ServerPackages/ DevPackages/  are COMMITTED.
#   wally.lock                              is COMMITTED.
#   net/generated/                          is COMMITTED.
#   types/globalTypes.d.luau                is COMMITTED.
#   roblox.yml (selene's Roblox std)        is COMMITTED.
#
# Committing them makes builds deterministic and offline-resolvable, and means
# a fresh clone can typecheck before it can reach the network. If you add
# Packages/ to this file, every acceptance gate in AGENTS.md becomes a lie.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
